# Container support for the Project Infinity-X sm8150 kernel (raphael)
#
# Base tree : raphael-resources/android_kernel_xiaomi_sm8150 @ 16.2
#             Makefile 4/14/356/-openela-rc1 + defconfig CONFIG_LOCALVERSION="-perf"
#             == 4.14.356-openela-rc1-perf, the running kernel exactly.
#             (The shipped sha e24fbe0953aa is orphaned -- the branch was
#             force-pushed 2026-06-19, 13 days after that kernel was compiled.
#             Head is 6035a52657a2. Identify the tree by fingerprint, not sha.)
# Baseline  : infinityx/running.config, pulled from /proc/config.gz on the device.
#
# DO NOT BUILD THIS AGAINST LineageOS/android_kernel_xiaomi_sm8150 @ lineage-23.2.
# That was tried and bootlooped with reboot,bpfloader-failed. The tree compiles
# and boots, then dies in Android userspace, because it is a PRISTINE 4.14
# without the ACK android-4.14 eBPF backports:
#
#   include/uapi/linux/bpf.h    30,242 B, 15 prog types   (vs 135,278 B, 36 here)
#   BPF_PROG_TYPE_CGROUP_SOCK_ADDR / _SOCKOPT   absent
#   BPF_MAP_TYPE_DEVMAP_HASH                    absent
#   kernel/bpf/btf.c                            absent
#
# The ROM sets ro.bpf.kver_override=5.4.299 (LineageOS legacy-bpf-compat), so
# netbpfload believes it is on 5.4, skips the DEVMAP_HASH->HASH downgrade it
# applies only below 5.4, and asks for map type 25 / prog types 18 and 25.
# A pristine 4.14 answers -EINVAL, the loader aborts, and init reboots.
#
# NOTE THE FAILURE MODE: every CONFIG_BPF* symbol was byte-identical to the
# device's. A config diff cannot see a missing subsystem. Verify SOURCE
# capability, not config -- see Step 5b in scripts/build_kernel_infinityx.sh.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS SEPARATELY FROM docker.config
# docker.config targets the SOVIET-ANDROID tree, which panicked on this ROM
# (kernel_panic,fatal_exception). Keep the two fragments apart.
#
# Verified present in the running config, so NOT repeated here:
#   NAMESPACES UTS_NS NET_NS CGROUPS CGROUP_FREEZER CGROUP_SCHED CPUSETS MEMCG
#   KEYS VETH BRIDGE OVERLAY_FS NETFILTER NETFILTER_ADVANCED IP_NF_NAT NF_NAT
#   IP_NF_TARGET_MASQUERADE MODULES
#
# Confirmed missing on-device by functional test, not just by reading config:
#   /proc/self/ns/  showed only  cgroup mnt net uts   (no user, pid, ipc)
#   /proc/cgroups   showed no    pids, devices

# --- namespaces Docker requires ----------------------------------------------
CONFIG_USER_NS=y
CONFIG_PID_NS=y
CONFIG_IPC_NS=y

# --- cgroup controllers Docker requires --------------------------------------
CONFIG_CGROUP_PIDS=y
CONFIG_CGROUP_DEVICE=y

# --- misc Docker prerequisites -----------------------------------------------
CONFIG_POSIX_MQUEUE=y
CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_MATCH_ADDRTYPE=y

# --- nftables backend ---------------------------------------------------------
# Debian bookworm defaults to iptables-nft, so dockerd programs rules through
# the nft backend. 4.14 splits NAT/masquerade/redirect per address family: the
# generic NFT_NAT / NFT_MASQ / NFT_REDIR are inert without the *_IPV4/*_IPV6
# and NFT_CHAIN_NAT_* symbols. These spellings do not exist in modern kernels.
# NF_NAT_IPV6 gates the three IPv6 entries; without it olddefconfig drops them.
CONFIG_NF_TABLES=y
CONFIG_NF_TABLES_INET=y
CONFIG_NF_TABLES_IPV4=y
CONFIG_NF_TABLES_IPV6=y
CONFIG_NF_TABLES_NETDEV=y
CONFIG_NF_NAT_IPV6=y
CONFIG_NFT_NAT=y
CONFIG_NFT_MASQ=y
CONFIG_NFT_REDIR=y
CONFIG_NFT_CHAIN_NAT_IPV4=y
CONFIG_NFT_CHAIN_NAT_IPV6=y
CONFIG_NFT_CHAIN_ROUTE_IPV4=y
CONFIG_NFT_CHAIN_ROUTE_IPV6=y
CONFIG_NFT_MASQ_IPV4=y
CONFIG_NFT_MASQ_IPV6=y
CONFIG_NFT_REDIR_IPV4=y
CONFIG_NFT_REDIR_IPV6=y
CONFIG_NFT_CT=y
CONFIG_NFT_COMPAT=y
CONFIG_NFT_COUNTER=y
CONFIG_NFT_LOG=y
CONFIG_NFT_LIMIT=y
CONFIG_NFT_META=y
CONFIG_NFT_REJECT=y
CONFIG_NFT_REJECT_INET=y
CONFIG_NFT_REJECT_IPV4=y
CONFIG_NFT_REJECT_IPV6=y
CONFIG_NFT_SET_HASH=y
CONFIG_NFT_SET_RBTREE=y
CONFIG_NFT_SET_BITMAP=y

# --- KernelSU-Next and SUSFS: DELIBERATELY NOT SET HERE -----------------------
# Both are already IN the tree, and the base config already enables them.
#
# Everything this section used to do -- bolting KernelSU-Next onto a tree that
# lacked it, choosing a tag, and planning a second pass to graft SUSFS in -- was
# an artefact of building from the WRONG SOURCE. On the ROM's own tree:
#
#   drivers/kernelsu/   in-tree, KSU_GIT_VERSION := 3131 hardcoded in its
#                       Makefile (no .git needed, so no fallback-to-1 hazard).
#                       KSU_VERSION = 30000 + 3131 + 150 = 33281, tag v3.2.0,
#                       manager hash 79e590113c4c... (KernelSU-Next official key)
#   fs/susfs.c          in-tree
#
# and infinityx/running.config -- the base we seed from -- already carries
# KSU, KSU_MANUAL_HOOK and all 11 KSU_SUSFS_* symbols enabled.
# Listing them again here would only risk overriding the ROM's own choices.
#
# In particular do NOT re-add KSU_KPROBES_HOOK. The stock kernel ships
# KSU_MANUAL_HOOK enabled, and KernelSU-Next's own Kconfig says of the kprobes
# hook: "This should not be used on kernel below 5.10." This is a 4.14 kernel.
#
# NOTE ON PROSE IN THIS FILE: never begin a comment line with "# CONFIG_<name>"
# followed by '=' or a space. scripts/kconfig/merge_config.sh extracts symbols
# with
#     s/^\(# \)\{0,1\}\(CONFIG_[a-zA-Z0-9_]*\)[= ].*/\2/p
# which does not distinguish a directive from a sentence that merely mentions
# one. Two comment lines here previously tripped that and merge_config.sh
# "redefined" KSU and KSU_MANUAL_HOOK to the literal comment text. olddefconfig
# then dropped both to their Kconfig defaults, which happened to match the
# device -- luck, not correctness. Write symbol names without the CONFIG_
# prefix in prose, as above.
#
# Consequence for sequencing: there is no longer a "root + Docker now, SUSFS
# later" split. One build gets all three.

# --- build speed --------------------------------------------------------------
# LOCALVERSION_AUTO makes scripts/setlocalversion run `git status`, which takes
# ~154 s over the virtiofs bind mount and re-runs every build (Makefile's
# kernel.release target is FORCE). The build script exports LOCALVERSION
# explicitly, so turning this off costs only the -g<sha> suffix.
# CONFIG_LOCALVERSION_AUTO is not set

# Deliberately NOT touched, unlike the SOVIET build:
#   LTO_CLANG / THINLTO  - already off here, so no link memory spike
#   LLVM_POLLY           - absent from this tree, so no optimizer hang
#   SECTION_MISMATCH_WARN_ONLY - already =y, so modpost will not abort
#   FTRACE               - already =y and it compiles fine on this tree
